  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Toda Ram Bijaraniya S/O Shri Gopal Lal vs State Of Rajasthan (2024:Rj-Jp:47792) on 21 November, 2024 Author: Sameer Jain Bench: Sameer Jain [2024:Rj-Jp:47792] High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan Bench At Jaipur S.B. Civil Writ Petition No. 16318/2024 1. Rajesh Kumar S/o Shri Balbir Singh, Aged About 38 Years, Resident Of Hameerwas, Nhu, Jhunjhunu, Rajasthan, 333041. 2. Surendra Yadav S/o Shri Chotu Ram Yadav, Aged About 25 Years, Resident Of Ward No. 08, Gram Akhepura, Tehsil Dantaramgarh, Dheengpur, District Sikar, Rajasthan - 332601 . 3. Suresh Kumar S/o Shri Hari Ram, Aged About 30 Years, Resident Of Pur, Jalore, Rajasthan 343041. ----Petitioners Versus 1. Additional Chief Secretary (Acs), Department Of Medical And Health Services, Rajasthan. 2. Commissioner, Food Safety And Drug Control, Commissionerate Food Safety And Drug Control, Tilak Marg, C Scheme, Jaipur, Rajasthan. 3. Rajasthan Public Service Commission, Through Its Chairman, Ajmer, Rajasthan. ----Respondents Connected With S.B. Civil Writ Petition No. 5930/2024 Toda Ram Bijaraniya S/o Shri Gopal Lal, Aged About 37 Years, Resident Of Bijaraniya Ki Dhani, Vijaypura, Khoor/vijaypura, District Sikar, Rajasthan Pincode 332023 ----Petitioner Versus 1. State Of Rajasthan, Through Principal Secretary, Medical And Health Department, Govt. Of Rajasthan, Government Secretariat, Jaipur-302001. 2. Rajasthan Public Service Commission, Through Secretary, Jaipur Road, Ajmer, Rajasthan-305001. ----Respondents (Downloaded on 28/11/2024 at 09:52:52 PM) Toda Ram Bijaraniya S/O Shri Gopal Lal vs State Of Rajasthan (2024:Rj-Jp:47792) on 21 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/161090787/ 1 [2024:RJ-JP:47792] (2 of 5) [CW-16318/2024] For Petitioner(s) : Mr. Vikram Pratap Singh for Mr. Rajat Arora Ms. Nikitha Bhandari For Respondent(s) : Mr. Archit Bohra, AGC Mr. M.F. Baig HON'BLE MR. JUSTICE SAMEER JAIN Order 21/11/2024 1. S.B. Civil Writ Petition No. 5930/2024 is filed with following prayers:- (a) That this Hon'ble Court be pleased to issue writ of Mandamus or any other appropriate writ order or direction in the nature thereof and thereby, the respondent may be directed to accept the candidature of the petitioner on the post of Food Safety Officer as the petitioner secured marks in the merit list; (b) That the hon'ble court be pleased to reserved one seat in the selection process for the post of food safety officer to be allocated specifically for the petitioner, considering his eligibility, qualification and the injustice faced during the recruitment process; (c) Pass such other and further order(s) as may deem fit and proper and in the interest of justice and protect the rights and interests of persons with disabilities.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "Moreover, the degree specified in the advertisement and degree possessed by the petitioner, are of different fields and have no co-relation. Under Section 3 of the UGC Act, 1956.\""
  },
